WEBVTT

00:00:02.862 --> 00:00:06.342
Ooh. Okay a little left. Ooh.
Back the other way a bit.

00:00:06.542 --> 00:00:08.662
Ooh. Okay, that's it. Go! Don't do it.

00:00:08.822 --> 00:00:10.982
-Bailey!
-Okay, now! Now! Do it! Do it!

00:00:11.102 --> 00:00:13.302
-Time for your idea.
-Okay. What idea? (SCREAMS)

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.382
(SCREAMING)

00:00:20.622 --> 00:00:23.942
Okay. What do I do?
What would Dory do?

00:00:24.062 --> 00:00:26.462
Come on, cars, cars. I see cars.
Otters in front of cars.

00:00:26.582 --> 00:00:29.502
Cars have to stop.
Stop traffic! Cuddle party!

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.022
(OTTERS CHITTERING)

00:00:32.142 --> 00:00:33.102
Look out!

00:00:33.182 --> 00:00:34.182
(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:00:35.142 --> 00:00:36.702
They're so cute!

00:00:36.862 --> 00:00:39.742
Look at them! There must be one, two...

00:00:41.182 --> 00:00:42.222
(ALL GROANING)

00:00:43.182 --> 00:00:45.662
-What's going on, Dad?
-I don't know how.

00:00:45.822 --> 00:00:48.702
I don't know in what way, but I think
this has something to do with--

00:00:50.302 --> 00:00:51.342
(PANTING)

00:00:51.422 --> 00:00:55.182
-ALL: Dory!
-Water. Water. I need water.

00:00:55.342 --> 00:00:56.502
Are you crazy? How'd you get here?

00:00:56.902 --> 00:00:57.902
(GASPS)

00:00:57.982 --> 00:00:59.662
-BOTH: Dory!
-Oh!

00:00:59.782 --> 00:01:02.542
-I thought we'd never see you again.
-Aw, me too.

00:01:02.702 --> 00:01:05.782
But, darn it, no matter how hard I tried
I just couldn't forget you.

00:01:07.022 --> 00:01:09.462
I guess I missed the rest of my family
too much, huh?

00:01:09.582 --> 00:01:11.302
-We're family?
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:12.382 --> 00:01:13.862
Do you know what that feels like?

00:01:14.222 --> 00:01:17.382
(SIGHS) Yes, I know what that feels like.

00:01:18.382 --> 00:01:19.902
ALL: Aw!

00:01:20.062 --> 00:01:23.382
Hey! Hey, come on. Out of the truck.
Those aren't your fish. Shoo!

00:01:23.542 --> 00:01:26.102
-Oh no. There goes our ride.
-Back in the water. Come on.

00:01:26.222 --> 00:01:29.222
(VOCALIZING) Dory,
the traffic is starting to move.

00:01:29.862 --> 00:01:31.022
Leave it to me. I got this.

00:01:31.102 --> 00:01:33.982
(CLEARS THROAT) Ooo-roo. Ooo-roo.

00:01:34.062 --> 00:01:37.302
Becky! Becky, come back.
We need your help! Becky!

00:01:37.422 --> 00:01:39.182
-(BECKY SQUAWKING)
-(GASPS)

00:01:39.262 --> 00:01:40.462
Dory, follow me.

00:01:41.782 --> 00:01:45.102
No, no, wait. We don't have Dory!
No, no, Becky wait! Stop it.

00:01:45.302 --> 00:01:50.062
We need to go back. Becky, back!
Back, Becky! Loo-loo. Ooo-roo-roo.

00:01:50.182 --> 00:01:52.422
-(SCREAMS) Please don't eat us!
-Where's Dory?

00:01:52.582 --> 00:01:54.222
-Who are you?
-Jenny?

00:01:54.342 --> 00:01:55.542
-Marlin?
-Charlie?

00:01:55.622 --> 00:01:56.662
-Nemo? Thank you so much.
-(SQUAWKS)

00:01:56.742 --> 00:01:59.542
Thank you for taking care of Dory.

00:01:59.702 --> 00:02:01.622
Dory! She's still in the truck.

00:02:01.822 --> 00:02:05.582
Becky! Fetch Dory! Ooo-roo. Dor-roo.

00:02:05.742 --> 00:02:06.742
(BECKY SQUAWKING)

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:11.262
Okay, kid. I guess this is goodbye.

00:02:11.382 --> 00:02:12.622
-No!
-What do you mean, "No"?

00:02:12.782 --> 00:02:15.222
You're not going to the Cleveland.
You are coming to the ocean with me.

00:02:15.302 --> 00:02:16.942
What is it with you
and ruining my plans?

00:02:17.022 --> 00:02:20.102
Listen to me, I have one goal in life.
One! And it is to--

00:02:20.262 --> 00:02:23.902
No, you listen to me. What is so great
about plans? I never had a plan.

00:02:23.982 --> 00:02:27.582
Did I plan to lose my parents? No.
Did I plan to find Marlin? No.

00:02:27.742 --> 00:02:30.382
Did you and I plan to meet?
Wait. Did we?

00:02:30.502 --> 00:02:32.662
-Are you almost done?
-Well, I don't think we did.

00:02:32.782 --> 00:02:35.622
And that's because the best things
happen by chance. Because that's life.

00:02:35.782 --> 00:02:40.342
That's you being with me out
in the ocean not safe in some glass box.

00:02:40.502 --> 00:02:41.502
-Can I say something?
-I'm not done!

00:02:41.622 --> 00:02:44.822
A friend of mine-- Her name's
Sigourney-- Once told me that...

00:02:44.982 --> 00:02:46.462
all it takes is three simple steps:

00:02:46.622 --> 00:02:50.022
Rescue, rehabilitation,
and one other thing--

00:02:50.182 --> 00:02:52.182
ALL: Release! (CHEERING)

00:02:52.302 --> 00:02:54.462
That's right! So what do you say?

00:02:54.662 --> 00:02:57.622
ALL: (CHANTING)
Release! Release! Release!

00:02:57.782 --> 00:03:01.062
Release! Release! Release!

00:03:01.182 --> 00:03:03.742
-Release! Release! Release!
-(SQUAWKING)

00:03:03.822 --> 00:03:05.622
I was gonna say, "Okay."

00:03:07.702 --> 00:03:09.022
Not good.

00:03:09.382 --> 00:03:11.342
JENNY: Oh no! They're going away!
NEMO: Oh no! Dory! What do we do?

00:03:11.462 --> 00:03:12.982
Quick! Guys, grab my fin!

00:03:15.142 --> 00:03:18.822
Ooh! He's trying to get the door open.
Ooh. It's locked from the outside.

00:03:18.942 --> 00:03:20.182
Come on, Dory. You can do it.

00:03:20.342 --> 00:03:22.662
Destiny! Destiny! Wall! Wall! Wall!

00:03:22.782 --> 00:03:23.942
(DESTINY SCREAMS)

00:03:24.022 --> 00:03:26.542
MARLIN: Dory, no! Wait!
DESTINY: Dory!

00:03:27.222 --> 00:03:30.742
-Bailey, where are they headed?
-Ooh. I'm losing them.

00:03:32.022 --> 00:03:33.382
(DOOR HANDLE CLICKING)

00:03:35.142 --> 00:03:37.102
Dory, it's over.

00:03:37.342 --> 00:03:40.342
-No, there's got to be a way.
-ALL: Yeah. There's a way!

00:03:40.542 --> 00:03:43.142
Dory, now listen to me.
There's no way to get out.

00:03:43.342 --> 00:03:45.662
But-- There's got to be a way.
There's always a way.

00:03:46.222 --> 00:03:49.542
There isn't, Dory. I'm telling you.
This time there is no other way.

00:03:50.022 --> 00:03:51.062
Well, what about that?

00:03:53.262 --> 00:03:55.022
Holy carp. There is another way.

00:03:55.422 --> 00:03:57.622
(EXHALES) Take a deep breath, kid.

00:03:57.742 --> 00:04:00.062
ALL: (CHANTING)
Release! Release! Release!

00:04:00.222 --> 00:04:03.822
Release! Release! Release! Release!

00:04:06.462 --> 00:04:07.982
♪ Your lying eyes... ♪

00:04:08.062 --> 00:04:09.302
(SCREAMING)

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:11.102
CARL: What is that?

00:04:11.182 --> 00:04:12.422
DAISY: I don't care what it is!
Get it off!

00:04:12.782 --> 00:04:13.662
What the--

00:04:14.422 --> 00:04:15.902
Suck it, bipeds.

00:04:17.062 --> 00:04:20.302
All right, Hank, you've got seven arms--
I don't know. Just try something.

00:04:20.462 --> 00:04:21.702
-Okay. Here we go.
-(HONKING)

00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:27.022
-Huh? Hey! Stop. Stop. Wait! No!
-Hey! Hey! Stop. Wait. Oh no!

00:04:27.142 --> 00:04:29.902
-That's doing something.
-And we are moving. Good job, Hank.

00:04:30.022 --> 00:04:34.982
-Wait, wait, wait! Come on! Whoa!
-Hey! What? Hey! Stop! Wait. Wait.

00:04:35.102 --> 00:04:38.422
Listen, I'm not trying to tell you
how to drive. Certainly I can't do--

00:04:38.582 --> 00:04:40.262
I'm not in any position--
But could you go faster?

00:04:40.422 --> 00:04:42.062
(GRUNTS)

00:04:42.142 --> 00:04:43.422
No! No, no! No, no, no!

00:04:44.262 --> 00:04:45.262
-(TIRES SCREECHING)
-(GASPS)

00:04:45.902 --> 00:04:48.062
-Whoo!
-Hey! Give us our truck back!

00:04:48.182 --> 00:04:49.742
I can't see squat.
Which way are we going?

00:04:49.942 --> 00:04:53.862
Okay. Well, all the cars
are going left so go left.

00:04:53.982 --> 00:04:57.382
Gilman Street. Ashby Avenue. Powell.

00:04:57.462 --> 00:05:00.022
Gilman Street again. Huh.
Gilman Street again.

00:05:00.102 --> 00:05:01.942
How much longer
are we gonna veer left?

00:05:05.622 --> 00:05:07.502
Okay, we just need to know
how we got on,

00:05:07.582 --> 00:05:08.902
then we'll know how to get off.

00:05:09.022 --> 00:05:10.582
Well, let me know
when you figure it out.

00:05:10.702 --> 00:05:12.302
Unfortunately I can't remember
how we got on.

00:05:12.462 --> 00:05:15.382
(GASPS) Hey, I know those guys!
That's where we came from. Turn right.

00:05:15.502 --> 00:05:16.422
Here we go!

00:05:17.102 --> 00:05:18.302
(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:05:19.462 --> 00:05:20.462
(ALL SCREAM)

00:05:21.262 --> 00:05:25.622
-Hey! Hey, hey, hey! Wait!
-Oh my-- Whoa. Hey!

00:05:26.142 --> 00:05:27.942
DAISY: We are so fired.

00:05:28.502 --> 00:05:32.902
DORY: Keep straight. Straight. Left.
Left. No, no, no. Right. Right. Right.

00:05:33.982 --> 00:05:36.062
-Good driving, Hank.
-Pay attention to the road.

00:05:36.182 --> 00:05:38.422
Oh, I'm sorry. Oh. Uh-oh.
Fork in the road.

00:05:38.542 --> 00:05:40.942
-Which way?
-Ocean. Ocean. Hey, a boat!

00:05:41.062 --> 00:05:42.902
You know, I haven't had
great experiences with boats, but I--

00:05:43.022 --> 00:05:46.062
-Which way?
-Boats go to the ocean. Right!

00:05:46.142 --> 00:05:47.462
Hold on!

00:05:47.542 --> 00:05:48.702
(ALL SCREAM)

00:05:51.062 --> 00:05:52.222
We're out of time, kid.
Where do we go now?

00:05:52.382 --> 00:05:55.502
Um... Okay, I'll figure it out.
I don't know, but--

00:05:55.582 --> 00:05:57.822
Well, something
will come and-- (GASPS)

00:05:58.342 --> 00:06:02.382
Seagulls. Hank, follow those birds!
The ocean's left, Hank.

00:06:03.582 --> 00:06:05.422
SEAGULLS:
Mine, mine, mine, mine.

00:06:05.542 --> 00:06:08.662
Ooh. Hold on. Ooh.
I'm getting something.

00:06:08.862 --> 00:06:10.182
Is it them? Is everything perfect?

00:06:10.342 --> 00:06:13.862
Uh-oh, it's the fuzz. Busted.

00:06:13.942 --> 00:06:15.182
(SIRENS WAILING)

00:06:17.382 --> 00:06:20.862
Okay, we're good. The ocean!
It's straight ahead. Floor it!

00:06:21.022 --> 00:06:21.982
Now we're talking.

00:06:24.222 --> 00:06:26.662
-Oh. Uh-oh!
-What do you mean, "Uh-oh"?

00:06:26.782 --> 00:06:29.222
Oh no. What would I do?
What would I do? What would I do?

00:06:30.222 --> 00:06:32.622
Hank, I'm gonna ask you
to do something crazy.

00:06:32.742 --> 00:06:34.422
I'm okay with crazy.

00:06:35.102 --> 00:06:36.342
All right, Hank.

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:40.502
Ooh. There's no way out. It's over.
They're going to fish jail! Ooh!

00:06:40.662 --> 00:06:45.662
Wait. Ooh. Oh no. Ooh.
Get back! Incoming!

00:06:46.702 --> 00:06:47.702
(DORY AND HANK SCREAMING)

00:06:48.222 --> 00:06:50.862
♪ I see trees of green

00:06:53.342 --> 00:06:55.822
♪ Red roses too

00:06:56.382 --> 00:06:58.982
♪ I see them bloom for me and you

00:07:01.662 --> 00:07:04.302
♪ And I think to myself ♪

00:07:04.422 --> 00:07:05.422
(ALL CHEERING)

00:07:07.622 --> 00:07:08.622
Whoo-hoo!

00:07:09.222 --> 00:07:10.222
Whoo-hoo!

00:07:10.622 --> 00:07:11.622
Whoo-hoo!

00:07:11.742 --> 00:07:12.742
(SNEEZES)

00:07:15.062 --> 00:07:16.582
Whoo-hoo!

00:07:18.222 --> 00:07:21.262
Fish!

00:07:22.062 --> 00:07:23.222
(BOTH GROANING)

00:07:24.902 --> 00:07:27.542
(IN SLOW MOTION) Dory!

00:07:27.622 --> 00:07:29.302
SIGOURNEY: What lies before you

00:07:29.382 --> 00:07:31.502
represents the third
and final part of the...

00:07:32.262 --> 00:07:33.902
Marine Life mission.

00:07:34.062 --> 00:07:39.222
Rescue, rehabilitation, and release.

00:07:39.982 --> 00:07:41.782
Come to Papa.

